# V10W1MjLines — what the five wave-1 goddesses say at the mahjong tables (lane 4, wave 1; data only, never gated
# here: V10Wave1.released() gates every consumer through the hooks in V10W1Mj).
#
# Each table mirrors the founders' table of its consumer key for key:
#   STAGE   ↔ V10MjStageLines.LINES      [subtitle (Russian, ≤ 32 characters), voiced text (Japanese, like every
#                                         heroine line since 0.7)]; 8 match events × 3 variants + 8 table events × 1
#   RIICHI  ↔ V10MjRiichiBarks.LINES     10 table events, the 8 shared with STAGE say the same words
#   KOIKOI  ↔ V10MjKoikoiLines.LINES     8 kinds; «koikoi / take / month» are the call words every rival shares
#   TRIPLES ↔ V10MjTriplesPresence.LINES 7 kinds
#
# Voice: no files yet. The voice path of a line follows the founders' pattern with her own id
# (assets/v10/mj/stage/voice/<hero>_<event>_<n>.ogg, assets/v10/mj/koikoi/voice/<hero>_<key>.ogg), so the subtitle
# plays alone until the audio lane records her. Rules (checked by V10W1Mj.selftest()): no V10Lint.BANNED stems, no
# UX_RULES §4.3 words, no mahjong jargon in Russian, never money, never guilt, flirt only toward the player.
#
# Voices: Цубамэ — cool courier, crisp, «Доставлено.»; Миэль — sunny pastry chef, «Попробуй!»; Кохаку — haughty
# teasing fox, «Удача любит меня»; Ширин — mysterious dancer, speaks in signs, «Звёзды не лгут»; Злата — regal and
# warm firebird tsarevna, «Весна пришла!».

